{
    "word": "lateen",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c810c6e5-c190-305b-9486-2494736c89ab",
                "word": "lateen",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f468a3b1-bd28-43b9-a8be-7321bd41c7ac",
                        "entry_id": "c810c6e5-c190-305b-9486-2494736c89ab",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lateens"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f67c112c-be3b-35d5-b6ac-41147a93e2be",
                        "entry_id": "c810c6e5-c190-305b-9486-2494736c89ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A triangular fore-and-aft sail set on a boom in such way that the tack is attached to the hull of the vessel and the free end of the boom lifts the sail."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f23f9b34-9576-4de5-bb41-e9b7a1f744c7",
                                "sense_id": "f67c112c-be3b-35d5-b6ac-41147a93e2be",
                                "text": "The shape of the lateen sail is triangular, or precisely that of a large fore-sail; it requires a long tapering yard to spread it, which will slightly bow or bend towards the middle when a stiff breeze fills the sail; a boom is used for some lateen sails, but not for all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf8a4ea5-0b97-4cde-918c-ff7c913ea079",
                                "sense_id": "f67c112c-be3b-35d5-b6ac-41147a93e2be",
                                "text": "Not only is its supporting and controlling rigging best suited to that sail position but, even more important, the sail itself thus presents a rigid leading-edge: the mast, in the case of most modern sailboats, or the yardarm to which the sail is attached, in the case of the medieval Mediterranean lateen or the modern Sailfish.\nFore-and-aft rigs come in a variety of shapes, but the medieval Mediterranean lateen was triangular, and this too was an asset."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4bf4103-0441-4600-9e3e-b15d17b4b7b3",
                                "sense_id": "f67c112c-be3b-35d5-b6ac-41147a93e2be",
                                "text": "The lateen sail is triangular or a quadrilateral which is almost triangular, the former being the type used by the Byzantines."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07e924b4-8545-4ea6-b332-0c9efcd0e9c1",
                                "sense_id": "f67c112c-be3b-35d5-b6ac-41147a93e2be",
                                "text": "1995, George F. Hourani, John Carswell, Arab Seafaring in the Indian Ocean in Ancient and Early Medieval Times, Princeton University Press, Expanded Edition, page 103,\nThe mere fact that this type of lateen no longer exists in the Mediterranean proves nothing; it is always possible that it might have originated there and later given way there to the still superior triangular form. But there are more substantial reasons for believing that the lateen came from the Indian Ocean to the Mediterranean. The earliest evidence of the existence of lateens in the Mediterranean is in Greek Byzantine manuscripts of the late ninth century, which show drawings of lateens (Plates 5 and 6)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e5b84502-fe04-439a-a112-42c09802b409",
                        "source_entry_id": "c810c6e5-c190-305b-9486-2494736c89ab",
                        "source_sense_id": "f67c112c-be3b-35d5-b6ac-41147a93e2be",
                        "source_sense_description": "sail",
                        "target_lang_word": "voile latine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "voile latine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc92ed74-b762-3dd5-8cd8-2bbeea96485b",
                                        "entry_id": "fe79e449-dfc0-35d1-bd5c-e35b092ce005",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Voile faite en forme de triangle, qui était en usage principalement sur la Méditerranée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2357e14-2b32-4bfc-965d-921c00d12d30",
                                                "sense_id": "cc92ed74-b762-3dd5-8cd8-2bbeea96485b",
                                                "text": "[…], j’ai failli être victime d’un de ces courants d’air inattendus ; notre bateau a été sur le point de se coiffer fort désagréablement, à cause d’une petite voile latine que j’avais imprudemment fait laisser ouverte, par amour du pittoresque."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f900ca51-181f-42f8-841e-75e5701ca0d1",
                                                "sense_id": "cc92ed74-b762-3dd5-8cd8-2bbeea96485b",
                                                "text": "Des barques avec des voiles latines posées en ciseaux descendaient et remontaient le cours du fleuve sous le même vent, phénomène que je n’ai jamais bien compris, quoiqu’on me l’ait expliqué plusieurs fois."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29855e6d-6da2-47ee-96b1-dfe6258240fb",
                                                "sense_id": "cc92ed74-b762-3dd5-8cd8-2bbeea96485b",
                                                "text": "Dans l’effacement universel, au milieu du lac, la voile latine de la grande barque de promenade se détachait, nette et vigoureuse, sur la lueur de braise du couchant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5aa8b75c-b125-4603-a326-162696760c30",
                        "source_entry_id": "c810c6e5-c190-305b-9486-2494736c89ab",
                        "source_sense_id": "f67c112c-be3b-35d5-b6ac-41147a93e2be",
